fferences across all outcome pairs, and prefers the lottery with the more favorable (higher) sum. The sum is not symmetric and depends on the order. Given the ambiguity, the reason is not clearly applicable in a straightforward way. But it is conceptually applicable because the outcomes and their differences are defined and computable. Thus, the decision reason can be applied to the decision problem.",
